[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526284093,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526478495,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526485698,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526488688,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526491196,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526493559,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526495995,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526498522,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526502137,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526505606,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526508974,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526512617,"data":"| Kaggle CPU kernel (the default) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer whose widest density matrix stays below `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS`, and the CI gate shards (`kaggle_run.py shards`) | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526518725,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU, `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4`) | simulations whose widest density matrix reaches `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` | IBM jobs; narrow replays the CPU runs faster |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526522636,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.52652629,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. Batch pushes requesting either ID ran on 4-core CPU machines without libtpu, so this account reaches no TPU through the CLI | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526530248,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526533786999998,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 15 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526538105,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526540817,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526543482,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526545719,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526547959,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526550193,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526552532,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526554815,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526557184,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526582947,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526588077,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526597548,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack. The kernel fetches the eight\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526600224,"data":"   pinned archives (sha256-checked), installs them through the PKGBUILD\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526602634,"data":"   recipes in `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`, runs `--extract`, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526604986,"data":"   stops with exit code 3 unless the regenerated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526607251,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json` equals the retained bytes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526609683,"data":"   The build host passes the same test against its Arch packages, so a run\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.52661225,"data":"   that reaches its entry used the same algebra code as the host.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526614725,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526617154,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526619437,"data":"4. The entry's stdout, stderr, exit code and changed files.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526621874,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526668477,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526672253,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526674467,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526676867,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526679067,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526681368,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526683803,"data":"| qiskit-ibm-runtime | 0.50.0 (fake backends such as FakeFez; no account or credential) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526686277,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526688824,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526697734,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI (Cayley-Calculator runtime) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526701652,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526705646,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526709242,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526712976,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526716196,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526719459,"data":"- A kernel is private, has internet enabled (and a GPU when one is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.52672329,"data":"  requested), and holds no IBM credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526727211,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526731058,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE`, which the kernel sets to its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526734872,"data":"  machine's device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526738463,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526742289,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526751414,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526754702,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526757312,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526759637,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526762057,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526764474,"data":"- An entry whose output a CI gate recompiles runs with `push --ci-env` on a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526766849,"data":"  CPU or GPU machine, using CPU Aer either way. The kernel then builds CI's Python 3.14.7 with CI's pins\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526769249,"data":"  through `ci/install_pins.sh` and runs the entry under it, because the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526771551,"data":"  image's Python 3.13 and numpy 2.1.3 change compiled depths and durations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526773944,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526776347,"data":"## Aer on the GPU\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526778723,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526780973,"data":"- **Requesting a GPU.** Push with `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4` and a `--timeout`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526783516,"data":"  sized to the work; kaggle_run.py refuses an accelerator push without one.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526785851,"data":"  The kernel installs qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 0.17.2 and sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.52678816,"data":"  `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE=GPU`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526790397,"data":"- **Using it in an entry.** The entry passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526793051,"data":"  `calibration_snapshot.aer_device()` to `noise_simulator(snapshot, device,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526796902,"data":"  method=...)`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526800942,"data":"- **Noise model width.** Restricting the snapshot and the circuit to the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526804928,"data":"  active qubits (`snapshot_laws.restrict` and `restrict_circuit`) keeps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526808689,"data":"  Aer's noise model at the circuit's width on either device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526812765,"data":"- **What the GPU is for.** It pays for density matrices at\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526816689,"data":"  `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` (11) qubits or more and for wide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526820646,"data":"  statevectors. Small dynamic circuits sample faster on the host CPUs. On\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526824392,"data":"  the 7-qubit N=21 order-finding circuits, statevector trajectories took 2.8\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526828422,"data":"  and 36 ms per shot on the CPU, against 21.7 and 54.6 ms on one T4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526832189,"data":"- **Batched shots.** `noise_simulator(..., batched_shots=True)` enables Aer's\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526835926,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`, which aborts on any circuit with control flow\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526839712,"data":"  (`if_else` lowers to `jump`), so only static circuits may batch. Batched\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526843423,"data":"  static runs are unmeasured here.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526847271,"data":"- **Replay.** A GPU's seeded counts differ from the CPU's. Its records are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526853179,"data":"  replayed from their retained counts, never by resampling on CI.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526855564999998,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526857903,"data":"The measurements are in `docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md`, from\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526860306,"data":"`results/kaggle/2026-10-16T204620Z-gororoba-aer-gpu-probe`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":23.526862648,"data":"\n"}
